From: Armada <no-reply@armadaos.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno,tu: minimum image size for mutable UBWC

On A740, keeping UBWC on every mutable image breaks some games. Truxton
Extreme creates a 64x64 R16G16B16A16_UNORM image (format list unorm,
snorm, uint, sint, float), renders into it through a FLOAT view each
frame, then reads it with vkCmdCopyImageToBuffer, which uses the image's
UNORM format. UBWC data written as FLOAT doesn't decode as UNORM, so the
copy returns garbage and the game's overlays and bloom come out black or
white. Marking the image is_mutable doesn't help on A740. A722 runs the
same sequence and decodes it correctly, so this is an A740 limitation.
Full-screen render targets with the same format list are fine, since
games write and read them through one format, and those are where UBWC
pays off: Platypus Reclayed's 1920x1080 RGBA16 targets run about 30%
faster with UBWC than without.

So with TU_Z_MUTABLE=2, a mutable image only keeps UBWC if its width times
height is at least the GPU's new mutable_ubwc_min_pixels property. Smaller
images stay tiled without UBWC, as with TU_Z_MUTABLE=1.

  - default 0: every size keeps UBWC (A722 and A650 are fine this way)
  - FD740 (A740, Adreno X1-85) sets 65536, i.e. 256x256

TU_Z_MUTABLE_MIN_PIXELS=<pixels> overrides the property on any GPU, for
example 0 to drop the limit when testing a game.
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_dev_info.h b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_dev_info.h
index 18717e2..89040a0 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_dev_info.h
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_dev_info.h
@@ -442,6 +442,11 @@ struct fd_dev_info {
        */
       bool storage_ubwc_internal_quirk;
 
+      /* Under TU_Z_MUTABLE=2, MUTABLE_FORMAT images keep UBWC only if
+       * they have at least this many pixels (0: any size).
+       */
+      uint32_t mutable_ubwc_min_pixels;
+
       /* Whether CP_ALWAYS_ON_COUNTER only resets on device loss rather than
        * on every suspend/resume.
        */
diff --git a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
index 040c423..ff6df12 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
+++ b/src/freedreno/common/freedreno_devices.py
@@ -1289,7 +1289,7 @@ add_gpus([
         GPUId(chip_id=0xffff43050c01, name="Adreno X1-85"),
     ], A6xxGPUInfo(
         CHIP.A7XX,
-        [a7xx_base, a7xx_gen2],
+        [a7xx_base, a7xx_gen2, GPUProps(mutable_ubwc_min_pixels = 65536)],
         num_ccu = 6,
         tile_align_w = 96,
         tile_align_h = 32,
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
index b3ba154..f9e7144 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_image.cc
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
 #include "tu_wsi.h"
 
 DEBUG_GET_ONCE_NUM_OPTION(tu_z_mutable, "TU_Z_MUTABLE", 2)
+DEBUG_GET_ONCE_NUM_OPTION(tu_z_mutable_min_pixels, "TU_Z_MUTABLE_MIN_PIXELS", -1)
 
 uint32_t
 tu6_plane_count(VkFormat format)
@@ -631,7 +632,18 @@ tu_image_init(struct tu_device *device, struct tu_image *image,
             force_linear_tile = true;
          } else if (!mutable_ubwc_fc) {
             int64_t z_mutable = debug_get_option_tu_z_mutable();
-            if (ubwc_enabled && z_mutable < 2) {
+            /* A740 can't decode UBWC written through one format and read
+             * through another (a FLOAT render target copied out as UNORM),
+             * so there only render-target-sized images keep UBWC.
+             */
+            int64_t z_min_pixels = debug_get_option_tu_z_mutable_min_pixels();
+            if (z_min_pixels < 0)
+               z_min_pixels = device->physical_device->info->props.mutable_ubwc_min_pixels;
+            bool z_keep_ubwc =
+               z_mutable >= 2 &&
+               (int64_t)image->vk.extent.width * image->vk.extent.height >=
+                  z_min_pixels;
+            if (ubwc_enabled && !z_keep_ubwc) {
                if (fmt_list && fmt_list->viewFormatCount == 2) {
                   perf_debug(
                      device,
